        <h2>Detect the Unseen.</h2>
        <p class="feature-kicker">Anomaly Detection · Isolation Forest</p>
        <p class="feature-body">
          Industrial equipment rarely fails without warning. Subtle deviations in vibration
          patterns can reveal changes in machine behaviour long before they become obvious.
          Maint-IQ identifies unusual patterns in engineered sensor features, helping direct
          attention toward signals that warrant investigation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-panel" data-state="predict">
        <p class="feature-index">02 — 04</p>
        <h2>Anticipate the Risk.</h2>
        <p class="feature-kicker">Failure Prediction · XGBoost</p>
        <p class="feature-body">
          Reactive maintenance addresses problems after they emerge. Predictive models offer
          another perspective by assessing patterns associated with equipment failure. Maint-IQ
          uses machine-learning predictions to help distinguish conditions that may require
          closer inspection from expected operating behaviour.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-panel" data-state="explain">
        <p class="feature-index">03 — 04</p>
        <h2>Understand the Why.</h2>
        <p class="feature-kicker">Analytics explanations</p>
        <p class="feature-body">
          A prediction is only as useful as our ability to interpret it. Maint-IQ explains
          analytics graphs using the plotted data and model outputs, so flagged conditions can
          be investigated with clear observations and stated limitations.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-panel" data-state="horizon">
        <p class="feature-index">04 — 04</p>
        <h2>Look Beyond the Present.</h2>
        <p class="feature-kicker">Remaining Useful Life · Regression</p>
        <p class="feature-body">
          Maintenance planning depends not only on identifying degradation, but also on
          understanding how equipment condition may evolve. Remaining useful life estimation
          explores the relationship between observed machine features and potential
          degradation trajectories, supporting more informed maintenance planning.
        </p>
